romise not to tell my girlfriend  who's currently listening behind me  so did i sell the addiction thing enough  i hope so  because i also think it's a great  mechanic too let me break it down  the new characters can be so gorgeous to  look at even for  non-weebs i mean noel's design is  appealing to me because of her bulking  great sword  this isn't a simple reskin either joelle  is a tank-like build whose sword takes  time to swing to hit the target  but is rewarded with heavier damage  numbers joelle also has an overshield  option  which protects her and remains in place  when switching to another character  therefore impacting your gameplay  massively oh and if you didn't know her  element is earth which in the game is  called  geo we haven't even touched on hydro and  dendro elements which are water and  nature too  i'm unable to check right now but this  got me thinking should a situation arise  where you need hydro power  yet you do not have a character that has  that ability what happens  this is a question i intend to find the  answer to but right now i haven't played  enough to really know this  i'm hoping the game will allow for  free-to-play players to get through this  somehow  but i'm not completely certain right now  i'm only 15 hours in  as this is speculation and not fact  let's leave that point there  just note that new characters change the  way you play the game  here's a cool thing to note the gacha  system has free goals so to speak  especially if you get the game during  the first few weeks  keep checking your in-game emails and  you will receive gift wishes  after chatting with other players the  recommendation is to pick up the  beginner's wish  pack which guarantees noel the character  we just talked about  and this also guarantees a four-star  item every 10 wishes  hmm i can feel that this is a slippery  slope towards spending money  if that's good with you go crazy it's  your cash if it isn't  remember to check yourself before you  wreck 